# Stage 3 of Myth (TZX block 46, Scandinavia 500 AD, at $6C3F-$F03E): the annotations kit/mkgame.py writes src/stage3/*.asm from.
#
# The same engine as stage 1 (src/stage1/stage1.ann) assembled at other addresses, with stage 3's own enemies, rooms
# and graphics. A routine that does stage 1's job keeps stage 1's name; tools/stage_names.py found 194 of stage 1's
# 310 routines here with the same code. The resident part $F03F-$FFFF (src/resident) is named by its own .ann: its
# routines and variables are @equ here, with the names that part uses.
#
# Variables outside the block: the screen, the play buffer, the resident part's routines and tables, and the work space
# $FE08-$FE6B (InitStageState clears $FE08-$FE68 at the stage start).
@equ $4000 Screen 6144 ; the screen's pixels
@equ $4134 EnergyBarScreen ; the HUD's energy bar: screen row 1, pixel line 1, column 20
@equ $5800 Attributes 768 ; the screen's attributes
@equ $5B00 PlayBuffer 4415 ; the play buffer $5B00-$6CFF (its tail $6C3F-$6CFF is PlayBufferTail in the block): 18 character rows of 8 lines of 32 bytes, linear; also the unpack area of StageGraphics
@equ $F959 DigitGlyphs ; resident font from '0': 8 bytes a character, 7 rows drawn (RenderDigits)
@equ $F9B0 PlaySoundVector ; resident: JP to the AY effect starter (E = the effect number)
@equ $F9BF DecimalTable 10 ; resident: the words 10000, 1000, 100, 10, 1
@equ $F9CB DissolveMasks 8 ; resident: the dissolve masks; DissolveHud reads sets 0-3 (32 bytes)
@equ $F9FB Score 2 ; resident: the score's low four decimal digits, 0-9999 (AddScore)
@equ $F9FD ScoreHigh ; resident: the score's high two digits (ten thousands), 0-99 (AddScore)
@equ $FA00 BitReverse 256 ; resident: each byte with its bits reversed (the sprites drawn facing left)
@equ $FB00 ScreenLineTable 384 ; resident: the screen address of each of the 192 pixel lines (words)
@equ $FC90 KeyUp ; resident key reader: Z when UP is held (DEFINE KEYS / joystick patch its port and bit)
@equ $FC9F KeyDown ; resident key reader: Z when DOWN is held
@equ $FCAE KeyLeft ; resident key reader: Z when LEFT is held
@equ $FCBD KeyRight ; resident key reader: Z when RIGHT is held
@equ $FCCC KeyFire ; resident key reader: Z when FIRE is held
@equ $FCDB KeyHook ; resident: called before every key read (a RET, or the joystick / pause check DEFINE KEYS installs)
@equ $FE08 RandomSeed 2 ; NextSeed $8A17: seed = seed x 5 + $15 (a linear congruential step); $07CF at the stage start (InitStageState)
@equ $FE0A RandomPointer 2 ; Random $8A26: a pointer into the ROM ($0000-$3FFF), whose bytes are the random numbers; reseeded from R every 64 passes, $07CF at the stage start, $0D7A at each burst
@equ $FE0E SavedSP 2 ; ClearBuffer and CopyBuffer keep the caller's SP here while SP walks their buffers
@equ $FE10 InitOnly10 ; set to 2 by InitStageState; no stage-3 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE12 InitOnly12 ; set to 1 by InitStageState; no stage-3 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE14 WorkByte ; scratch: the placement counter of LoadRoomActors, the shape bits of StartBurst
@equ $FE17 ItemSelected ; the slot of CarriedItems the HUD cursor is on (6 at the start)
@equ $FE18 ItemLast ; the last used slot of CarriedItems (6 at the start; AddItem raises it)
@equ $FE19 ItemFirst ; the first slot of CarriedItems (6): the item window does not scroll before it
@equ $FE1C SpanCount 2 ; the spans in the span table SpanTable $76E0 that CopyBuffer copies (BuildSpans $99B1)
@equ $FE1E SpanRow ; BuildSpans' cell row 0-17
@equ $FE1F CellColumn ; the cell column 2-29 of RoomChange's and BuildSpans' loops
@equ $FE21 RoomColumn ; the room's left edge in the grid, in blocks (2 cells)
@equ $FE22 RoomRow ; the room's top edge in the grid, in blocks (16 lines)
@equ $FE23 RoomGrid 2 ; the grid record of the current map grid (Grid0 $9B37, Grid1 $9B44 or Grid2 $9B58)
@equ $FE25 Placements 2 ; the current grid's placement list (Grid0Placements, Grid1Placements, Grid2Placements): 3 bytes a placement, $FF ends
@equ $FE27 MissileCursor ; AddMissile's round-robin slot number 0-7
@equ $FE29 CellFlag ; PutBlock $994E: the byte written to the cell's twin in $7040 (always 0)
@equ $FE2E RoomExitsPtr 2 ; the current room's byte in the grid's room table (grid record +4 + RoomNumber)
@equ $FE30 RoomNumber ; the room in its grid, a grid row of rooms after another: +1 right, -1 left, + grid record +8 down (grid 1: 8 the dragon's room, 10 the drawbridge's)
@equ $FE31 PassCounter ; +1 every pass (PassTick $9815): the animations' clock
@equ $FE3A InitOnly3A ; set to $10 by InitStageState; no stage-1 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE3D BurstTimer ; the burst's step 0..$1B ($0D in the small mode); $64 idle (RoomChange sets it), $FF just started
@equ $FE3E BurstSmall ; 0 a big burst (28 steps), 1 a small one (14 steps, doubled direction steps)
@equ $FE3F Energy ; the hero's energy, 0 (empty: a life lost) to $2E (full)
@equ $FE41 InitOnly41 ; set to $0D by InitStageState; no stage-3 code reads it (stage 1's InitOnly40; known only from the code)
@equ $FE42 InitOnly42 ; set to 1 by InitStageState; no stage-3 code reads it (stage 1's InitOnly41; known only from the code)
@equ $FE43 SpanOpen ; (stage 1: $FE42) BuildSpans: 1 while a run of open cells goes on
@equ $FE4B ItemsChanged ; (stage 1: $FE4A) 1 after AddItem: the main loop redraws the item strip
@equ $FE4C GridNumber ; (stage 1: $FE4B) the grid the hero is in: 0 Grid0 (the longship), 1 Grid1 (the swamp, the forest, the dragon and the castle's drawbridge), 2 Grid2 (the castle's hall)
@equ $FE4D DragonHits ; the hits on the dragon (grid 1 room 8): DrawDragon $887A counts them, $0F the last; DragonBeaten $A00F sets $10 (dead); read by UpdateThrownAmmo, DragonFireDamage, DragonHeadActor, DragonFlameActor
@equ $FE4E DragonHitFlag ; 1 for one pass after a thrown object reaches the dragon (UpdateThrownAmmo $8058); DrawDragon counts the hit, paints the dragon red and clears it; DragonHeadActor turns red on it
@equ $FE4F DragonBreath ; the dragon's breath step, 0 or 1-$12, written by DragonHeadActor ($92FF); DragonFlameActor shows the flame at steps 4-$11, DragonFireDamage ($8819) hurts the hero while it is not 0
@equ $FE59 LightningState ; the longship's lightning: stepped by LightningStep $A588 (4 the calm), read by LightningActor $94AC for the bolt's shape
@equ $FE5A RainStep ; the rain's step: StartRain $A3BA starts it, UpdateRain $A41E counts it (step $50 and $64 move PyreState), StopRoomEffects $9F19 clears it
@equ $FE5B RainPointer 2 ; RainRandomByte $A54A's pointer through the ROM for the drops' columns; set by StartRain $A3BA
@equ $FE5C DrawbridgeDown ; set to 1 by DrawbridgeActor ($93BA) when the drawbridge has come down (frame 7); read by it at $9374
@equ $FE5D PyreState ; the funeral pyre: 0 burning, 1 the flames dying (rain step $50), 2 out (step $64), 3 the body rising, 4 gone (PyreBodyActor); also read by PyreFireDamage $87ED and the room changes $9D97, $9DD3
@equ $FE65 ThroneBossHits ; the hits on the giant on the throne (grid 2): ThroneBossStep counts them ($9564), $1E the last; ThroneBossBeaten $A02A sets $1F
@equ $FE66 ThroneHitFlag ; 1 when the hero's bolt reaches the giant (UpdateBolt $8239); ThroneBossStep reads it ($9530) and clears it ($955A)
@equ $FE68 VikingCount ; the Vikings on the longship, at most 4: SpawnViking +1 ($8C44, $8C59), VikingDie -1 ($8E85), StopRoomEffects $9F1D clears it
@equ $FE50 EnergyShown ; (stage 1: $FE4D) the energy the HUD bar last drew
@equ $FE51 EnergyChange ; (stage 1: $FE4E) the pending energy change: $80 and up drains 2 a pass, under $80 refills 2 a pass
@equ $FE52 SpawnDelay ; (stage 1: $FE4F) passes to the next random spawn (a random 0-15 at the stage start)
@equ $FE53 FireLatch ; (stage 1: $FE50) 1 while FIRE stays held after a shot or a throw: one a press
@equ $FE54 PiecesMask ; (stage 1: $FE51) one bit a piece of the artefact (the room event's bit, actor +$10): spawned and taken
@equ $FE55 PiecesTaken ; (stage 1: $FE52) pieces taken, 0-5
@equ $FE56 PieceFlash ; (stage 1: $FE53) passes left of the HUD pieces' colour flash
@equ $FE57 PiecesComplete ; (stage 1: $FE54) set to 1 when the fifth piece is taken; +1 for each item of kind 6 taken (SpawnRewardItem gives the kind-6 item while it is 1)
@equ $FE58 PieceTakenFlag ; (stage 1: $FE55) 1 for one pass after a piece is taken
@equ $FE5E RespawnShiftX ; (stage 1: $FE56) $FF: no death pending; else the hero's column less the respawn column less 2 (HeroDeath $B2C9); the path flyers move by it (x 2) when their path ends
@equ $FE5F RespawnShiftY ; (stage 1: $FE57) the hero's line less the respawn line less $27, set with RespawnShiftX
@equ $FE60 HeroFreeze ; (stage 1: $FE58) passes the hero's state handler is skipped ($17 after a life lost)
@equ $FE61 RestoreAttributes ; (stage 1: $FE5A) 1: UpdateAttributes takes the solid cells' colours from RoomAttributes once (the new room fades in over the old one)
@equ $FE62 LivesFlash ; (stage 1: $FE59) the lives boxes' flash step, 0-$10 ($10 idle)
@equ $FE63 GameOverTimer ; (stage 1: $FE5B) 0 in play; 1 when the last life is lost, counts to $32
@equ $FE64 InitOnly64 ; set to $0A by InitStageState; no stage-3 code reads it (stage 1's BossHits; known only from the code)
@equ $FE6B Lives ; (stage 1: $FE61) lives left, from H at StageEntry
@inline $8ADE 5
@inline $8B0E 5
@inline $AC0A

@module variables ; The stage's work space: the play buffer's tail, the shadow attributes, the HUD picture and the records over it
@about The block's first 5057 bytes ($6C3F-$77FF) are loaded with the stage but hold no code. $6C3F-$6CFF is the end of the play buffer PlayBuffer ($5B00-$6CFF: 18 character rows of 8 lines of 32 bytes, linear), $6D00-$6FFF the shadow of the screen's attributes. $7000-$76BF holds, as loaded, the HUD: its picture (48 lines of 32 bytes, linear) and its colours (6 rows of 32). StageSetUp $970D copies the colours into the shadow and dissolves the picture onto the screen (DissolveHud $8952); from then on the space is the stage's records: the old room's colours and the burst's particles ($7040), the room's cells ($7280), the hero's and the 13 other actors' records ($74E0, $74F2), the 16 missile records ($75E0), the digit picture ($7640); the span table starts at $76E0 (stage 1: $76A0). EndStage $78B6 saves the screen's HUD lines and colours back into $7000 and $7600 before the next stage's block is loaded over them. The layout is stage 1's but for the span table.
@about An actor record (18 bytes, the hero's at $74E0 and 13 at $74F2): +0 X (byte column 0-29; $FF a free record), +1 Y (line in the play buffer), +2 width in bytes, +3 height in lines, +4/+5 the frame's bitmap, +6/+7 the handler, +8 the frame or a counter, +9 flags (bit 0 opaque, bit 4 hit, bit 7 facing left), +$0A the state, +$0B the item kind or a step, +$0C the attribute, +$0D/+$0E the base X and Y (SetActorFrame $AC0A adds the frame's dx, dy to them), +$0F flags (bit 1 kept over a room change, bit 2 a body, bit 6 hidden, bit 7 drawn in the second pass), +$10 the placement's index or a counter, +$11 the pixel shift (drawn shifted by PreShiftSprite $7F43). As in stage 1.
$6C3F s PlayBufferTail ; The last 193 bytes of the play buffer PlayBuffer $5B00-$6CFF (character row 17's last lines)
> ClearBuffer $9A7D clears the play buffer to $6CFF with PUSH HL (SP from $6D00); RoomChange unpacks the stage's tiles and map into it from $5B00 (4437 bytes, to $6C54: StageGraphics); the actors are drawn into it every pass. Zero as loaded. Read and written in rzx-r3 and s3-right (all 193 bytes written in rzx-r3).
$6D00 s ShadowAttributes ; The shadow of the screen's 768 attributes, the screen's layout; the play area from $6DC2 (row 6, column 2)
> The HUD's colours are copied into rows 0-5 at the stage's set-up (StageSetUp $970D); RoomChange writes each cell's attribute into rows 6-23, the actors' colours are painted over them every pass, and UpdateAttributes copies the open cells to $5800 (ShowShadowAttributes $8B3E the whole of it). FillShadowAttributes $8B0E paints rectangles into it with five bytes after its CALL. The two big pictures paint their colour tables into it with $FF cells left alone: the dragon's at $6E92 (DragonAttributes, row 9 column 18) and the seated figure's at $6E59 (ThroneAttributes, row 9 column $19). Zero as loaded. All 768 bytes read and written in rzx-r3 and s3-right.
$6DC0 PlayAttributes ; row 6: the first row of the play area (the room's 18 rows)
$6DC2 PlayAttributesCell ; row 6, column 2: the room's first cell
$6E59 ThroneAttributesCell ; row 9, column 25: where the seated figure's colours (ThroneAttributes) go, 5 x 10 cells
$6E92 DragonAttributesCell ; row 9, column 18: where the dragon's colours (DragonAttributes) go, 9 x 9 cells
$7000 b HudPicture 32 ; The HUD as loaded: 48 lines of 32 bytes (linear, top first), then their colours at $7600 (6 rows of 32)
> DissolveHud $8952 dissolves the 48 lines onto the screen's lines 0-47 and StageSetUp $970D copies the 192 colours into the shadow rows 0-5, once, at the stage's start. EndStage $78B6 saves the screen's lines 0-47 back here ($791B) and the attributes $5800-$58BF to $7600 ($78CA), so the next stage's block shows the HUD as the player left it. Between the two the bytes are the records labelled inside (RoomAttributes, Cells, HeroRecord, Actors, Missiles, DigitBuffer). The picture: the frame of the HUD, the energy bar's box, the score box, the item strip's box, the lives and pieces boxes. All 1728 bytes read and written in rzx-r3 and s3-right.
$7040 RoomAttributes ; $7040-$727F: the old room's play colours (SavePlayAttrs: 576 bytes, rows 6-23) and the cells' twins ($7042 + row x 32 + column: PutBlock writes 0, UpdateAttributes reads the solid cells' colours); also the burst's particles (StartBurst $A169, 4 bytes each)
$7042 RoomAttributesCell ; the twin of the cell $7282 (576 bytes lower)
$7280 Cells ; the room's cells: 19 rows of 32 (tile numbers, then their kinds after BuildSpans; bit 1 solid, bit 3 deadly)
$7282 CellsPlay ; row 0, column 2: the room's first cell (RoomCells writes 28 x 18)
$73EE CellsDrawbridge ; row 11, column 14: the cells the drawbridge (kind 7, $9369) opens: written by it and by RoomChange, read by the hero's footing checks
$74C0 CellsFloor ; row 18 below the room: 32 bytes of $FF (StartGrid $A639), a floor no actor falls through
$74E0 HeroRecord ; the hero's actor record (18 bytes; +0 X)
$74E1 HeroY ; +1 the hero's line
$74E3 HeroHeight ; +3 the hero's height in lines ($16 at the stage's start, StageEntry)
$74E8 HeroFrame ; +8 the frame number of the hero's set
$74E9 HeroFlags ; +9 bit 7: facing left
$74EA HeroState ; +$0A 0 stand, 1 walk, 2 jump, 3 fall, ...; $0F dying (the hero's state handlers)
$74EC HeroAttribute ; +$0C the hero's attribute
$74ED HeroBaseX ; +$0D the base column ($0D at the stage's start)
$74EE HeroBaseY ; +$0E the base line
$74F0 HeroCounter ; +$10 the pause after a death (HeroDeath)
$74F2 Actors ; the 13 other actor records, 18 bytes each ($74F2-$75DB); +0 = $FF a free record
$74F3 ActorsY ; the first record's +1
$75CA LastActor ; the 13th record
$75DC ActorsEnd ; 4 bytes past the records: only the HUD picture's (DissolveHud, EndStage's save) bytes
$75E0 Missiles ; the 16 missile records, 6 bytes each ($75E0-$763F): +0 the column ($FF free), +1 the line, +2 the kind, +3 to +5 the kind's own
$75E1 MissilesY ; the first record's +1
$7600 HudColours ; the HUD's 192 colours as loaded (rows 0-5); in play the missile records 5 (its last 4 bytes) to 15 lie over them
$7610 MissilesHigh ; missile records 8-15 (the hero's death sparks)
$7611 MissilesHighY ; record 8's +1
$7640 DigitBuffer ; in play: the score's digit picture (6 + 2 columns x 8 lines, RenderScore $7B61) and a sprite's shifted copy (PreShiftSprite $7F43)
@res stage3/picture-hud-32x48.bin
$76C0 s Unused76C0 ; 32 bytes between the HUD's colours and the span table that no code reads or writes (rzx-r3, s3-right); zero as loaded
$76E0 s SpanTable ; The open spans CopyBuffer copies, 6 bytes each (the length, 0, the buffer address, the screen address; SpanCount spans), on to $77FF
> BuildSpans $99B1 and AddSpan $9A36 write the spans from here (stage 1 starts them at $76A0, over the HUD's colours; stage 3 keeps them clear of it); CopyBuffer $9AA2 reads them. rzx-r3 writes $76E0-$77A5 (33 spans), s3-right 26 spans; $77A6-$77FF (90 bytes) is never reached in the two recordings. Zero as loaded.

@module entry ; The stage's entry and set-up
$7800 c StageEntry ; Start the stage: lives from H, variables, HUD, the first room, the hero placed, then the main loop
> Called by the resident stage loader with H = the lives left. Stores H in Lives, then: InitStageState $9D00 (the variables, the carried items from StartItems), StageSetUp $970D (the title, the HUD), ClearActors $959F and ResetObjectLists $95B0, RoomGrid = $9B37 (grid 0, the longship) with Placements = $9B62 (grid 0's placements), ReviveAllPlacements $A69F and PlaceHeroAtStart $A672, GridNumber = 0, RoomNumber = 1, StartGrid $A639 (builds the room), ClearBuffer, RunActorHandlers $A7BB, DrawActors $A7DD and CopyBuffer, StageFadeIn $9785; then the hero record: $74E3 (+3, the height) = $16, the state $74EA = 0, the base column $74ED = $0D; runs on into MainLoop.
> Stage 1's StageEntry ($7800) has the same job but enters grid 0 at room 2, with no StageFadeIn call and no hero fields of its own (known from the code at $7826 and $7839-$7847).
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r3, s3-right).
$784A c MainLoop ; One pass: pace, HUD, input, actors, the stage's hazards, draw, copy; SPACE opens the item window
> The pass, in order: PacePass, ShowPieceTaken, FlashPieces, CheckPause (ENTER), SpawnTimer, RedrawItemsIfChanged, ClearBuffer, CheckStageExit (may leave to EndStage), $A3FD, $A41E, UpdateMissiles $B384, RunActorHandlers $A7BB, DrawActors $A7DD, DrawDragon (grid 1 room 8), $9514 (grid 2: the throne giant's picture and its fireballs), UpdateBurst $A201, KeyHook, $A588 (grid 0: the lightning), UpdateAttributes (attributes and CopyBuffer), PassTick $9815 (energy, lives flash, game over step), ShowScore, then the SPACE test TestSpaceKey.
> SPACE with CAPS SHIFT ends the stage with E = 1 (QuitStage); SPACE alone opens ItemWindow while HeroFreeze is 0. The loop goes on while Lives is not 0 or the hero's state $74EA is not 0; with no lives and the hero back in state 0 it runs on into GameOverExit (E = 0).
> Stage 1's MainLoop at $7839 has the same frame; it calls DrawArenaPicture, ZoneDamage and DrawRoomPicture where stage 3 calls DrawDragon, $9514 and $A588, and tests the hero's state $0F (not HeroFreeze) before the item window.
> Witness: L1 6279 (rzx-r3, s3-right).
$788E MainLoopSpace ; SPACE pressed: CAPS SHIFT too quits, else the item window while HeroFreeze is 0
$78A0 MainLoopNext ; go on while lives are left or the hero is not back in state 0

@module mainloop ; The main loop and its pass
$78AF c GameOverExit ; No lives: end the stage with E = 0
> Reached from MainLoop when Lives and the hero's state $74EA are both 0. E = 0, then EndStage.
> Stage 1's GameOverExit at $7897 is the same code.
> Witness: L1 1 (s3-right).
$78B4 c QuitStage ; CAPS SHIFT + SPACE: end the stage with E = 1
> Stage 1's QuitStage at $789C is the same code (LD E,1, then on into EndStage).
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: rzx-r3, s3-right); known only from the code.
$78B6 c EndStage ; Leave the stage: hide the HUD boxes, save the HUD, fade, return E, H = lives, BC = the score's digits
> E (pushed) is the outcome: 0 game over (GameOverExit), 1 quit (QuitStage), 2 stage completed (StageExit). Clears the play buffer, hides the pieces boxes and the lives boxes with two inline attribute fills ($8ADE), saves the HUD attributes (rows 0-5) to $7600, clears the score, the two middle HUD fields, the item strip and the pieces field with CopyToScreen from the cleared buffer (stride 0), saves the HUD bitmap (lines 0-47) to $7000 ($892A), fades the screen (FlashFadeScreen), clears it ($8A33), waits 100 frames ($8AD6) and returns to the stage loader with E, BC = ScoreDigitsHigh (the six score digits) and H = Lives.
> Stage 1's EndStage at $789E is the same code.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r3, s3-right).
$78BD b EndPiecesBox 5 ; FillAttributes' inline record: column 25, line 24, 6 x 2 cells, attribute 1 (the pieces boxes hidden)
> Read by FillAttributes $8ADE after the CALL at $78BA. Stage 1's EndPiecesBox at $78A5 holds the same bytes.
$78C2 c EndStageLives ; EndStage, continued: hide the lives boxes
> Part of EndStage, after the first inline record.
> Stage 1's EndStageLives at $78AA, the same instructions; the operand that differs is the CALL's at $78C2: stage 3's FillAttributes $8ADE.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r3, s3-right).
$78C5 b EndLivesBox 5 ; FillAttributes' inline record: column 1, line 24, 6 x 2 cells, attribute 1 (the lives boxes hidden)
> Read by FillAttributes $8ADE after the CALL at $78C2. Stage 1's EndLivesBox at $78AD holds the same bytes.
$78CA c EndStageSave ; EndStage, continued: save the HUD, clear its fields, fade, return
> Part of EndStage, after the second inline record.
> Stage 1's EndStageSave at $78B2 is the same code.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r3, s3-right).

@module render ; The renderer: the sprite row plotters, the play buffer, the attributes, ClearBuffer and CopyBuffer
$793D c FlashFadeScreen ; Fade every coloured ink up to white over 7 frames, then down to black over 7 frames
> Seven times (HALT each): every attribute whose ink is neither 0 nor 7 gets ink + 1. Then seven times (two HALTs each): every ink not 0 gets ink - 1. Inputs: none; changes the whole attribute area $5800-$5AFF. Called by EndStage.
> Stage 1's FlashFadeScreen at $7925 is the same code.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r3, s3-right).
$793F FadeUpFrame
$7947 FadeUpCell
$7951 FadeUpNext
$795C FadeDownFrame
$7965 FadeDownCell
$796B FadeDownNext

@module mainloop
$7975 c PacePass ; Reseed the random pointer every 64 passes and pad the pass with a busy wait in grid 1's room 10
> When PassCounter & $3F is 0, the high byte of RandomPointer is set from R. Then: in grid 1 (GridNumber 1), room 10 waits $044C rounds of DelayBC (it runs on into it); every other room goes on at once. Stage 1 waits in grid 0's rooms 0-5 and grid 1's room 0 (PacePass, PacePassUnused and PaceShaftRoom); stage 3 has only this test. The wait ran 120 times (rzx-r3).
> Witness: L1 6279 (rzx-r3, s3-right).
$7987 PacePassRoom ; grid 1 room 10 only

@module util ; Small helpers: keys, clears, copies, numbers, random numbers, delays
$7999 c DelayBC ; Busy wait: count BC down to 0
> Input BC (the rounds, 26 T-states each). Output BC = 0, A = 0. The interrupt returns land on its three instructions (L1 lists them as entries).
> Stage 1's DelayBC at $79AB is the same code.
> Witness: L1 132000 (rzx-r3).
$799A DelayBCTest
$799C DelayBCLoop

@module mainloop
$799F c CheckPause ; ENTER pauses: wait for its release, a second press and its release
> Reads port $BFFE bit 0 (ENTER). Not pressed: returns at once. Pressed: waits for the key's release, the next press and its release, so the game stands still between two presses. No other effect.
> Stage 1's CheckPause at $79B1 is the same code.
> Witness: L1 6279 (rzx-r3, s3-right).
$79A7 PauseRelease
$79AD PausePress
$79B3 PauseRelease2

@module render
$79BA c CopyToScreen ; Copy a block of bytes to the screen, line by line
> Inputs: HL = the source, B = the screen column, C = the first pixel line, D = the width in bytes, E = the lines, A = the source's stride (added to HL after each line; 0 repeats one source line, used with the cleared buffer to clear a screen block). Patches the column into $79D3 and the stride into $79E4, then for each line takes the line's address from ScreenLineTable and LDIRs D bytes. Destroys IX, BC, DE.
> Stage 1's CopyToScreen at $79CC is the same code.
> Witness: L1 7038 (rzx-r3, s3-right).
$79CD CopyToScreenLine

@module hud ; The energy, the lives, the score, the HUD, game over and the stage exit
$79EA c CheckStageExit ; Grid 1 room 2 with item 6 selected, the hero standing at columns 10-13: the stage's exit
> Returns unless GridNumber is 1, RoomNumber 2, the selected item (GetSelectedItem) of kind 6, the hero's column $74E0 10-13 and his state $74EA 0; then it runs on into StageExit (E = 2 at the end). Stage 1's CheckStageExit ($79FC) asks for grid 0 room 2 and BossPhase; stage 3 tests the grid. rzx-r3 ends the stage so (StageExit ran once; its screen 17128 shows the stars).
> Witness: L1 6279 (rzx-r3, s3-right).
$7A0B c StageExit ; The stage's exit effect: falling stars over a coloured field until FIRE or SPACE, then EndStage with E = 2
> StartStageExit draws the field and seeds 80 stars at $5B00 (4 bytes each); then each frame (HALT) moves the stars of speed 1-3 (MoveStar), until KeyFire or SPACE ($88F5); then E = 2 and EndStage.
> Stage 1's StageExit at $7A1D is the same code.
> Witness: L1 1 (rzx-r3).
$7A0F StageExitFrame
$7A16 StageExitStar
$7A33 StageExitDone
$7A38 c MoveStar ; Move one star down by its speed and plot it as two pixel lines
> IX = the star: +0 speed 1-4, +1 the pixel within the byte 0-3, +2 the column 2-29, +3 y ($80 and up: not yet on screen). Off screen: y += speed only. On screen: y = (y + speed) mod 128, clears the bytes above it (speed lines, from ScreenLineTable+96, line 48 down), and plots two lines from StarPixels (speed and pixel).
> Stage 1's MoveStar at $7A4A is the same code.
> Witness: L1 8004 (rzx-r3).
