@module enemies ; The enemies, the hazards and the bosses: the Vikings, the trolls, the bog men, the dragon, the pyre, the lightning, the giant on the throne
@about Grid 0 (the longship): Vikings (SpawnViking, VikingActor), the lightning (LightningStep, LightningActor), the rain and the sea (CheckWaterDeath). Grid 1 (the swamp and the forest): trolls in two records (SpawnTroll, TrollLegsActor, TrollBodyActor), bog men (SpawnBogMan, BogManActor), the funeral pyre (PyreFlameActor, PyreBierActor, PyreBodyActor: the rain puts the flames out and the body rises), the dragon in room 8 (DrawDragon, DragonHeadActor, DragonFlameActor; 16 thrown objects kill it) and the drawbridge (DrawbridgeActor). Grid 2 (the castle's hall): the giant on the throne (ThroneBossStep; 30 bolts kill it).
$82B9 c UpdatePieceActor ; Piece actor: takes 6 hits, rises, bobs and then waits to be taken as a piece of the artefact (1200 points)
> IY = the actor (18-byte record from PieceTemplate `$9C94`, spawned two at a time by SpawnBonus `$9F93`). Colour from the cycle (SetCycleColour `$B49C`). +$0B not 0 (the second record, the sparkle): frames 2-9 in turn (+8 + 1 AND 7, + 2). Else by +$0A: 6 PieceRises, 7 PieceWaitsPickup; 0-5: each hit (+9 bit 4, set by a shot or the hero's blow) clears the flag and adds 1 to +$0A; at 6 the next record's +0 is set to $FF (the sparkle freed). Frame 0. Draws with SetActorFrame (PieceActorSet: the frame table `$DFB3`, the set PieceSprites `$DECB`). Output: none.
