> LoadRoomActors $A6CA puts each placement not done that lies in the room's window into a free actor record, with the kind's row of ActorKinds; bit 7 of the kind is set when the actor is beaten or taken, so it does not come back (48 placement bytes written in each recording). Grid 0: four of kind $0C (at X 16, 56, 96, 144, line 0: the lightning) and ten of kind 4 (the sea at the foot of the hull, Y 15). Grid 1: 34 placements: kinds 0-3 (urns and chests, 11), kind 4 (the water of the swamp, 15), kind 5 (Y 6), 6 (Y 8), 7 (the drawbridge, X 234), 8 and 9 (two each, X 120-131: the dragon's room), $0A and $0B (X 124). Grid 2: none. Read in rzx-r3 (140 of the 153 bytes) and s3-right (72).
