$AA49 c SpawnFragments ; Start D fragment actors at column B, line C
> Seeds the random pointer RandomPointer $FE0A with $07CF (so every burst looks the same), writes B and C into the
> LD D / LD E at FragmentColumn $AA60 and FragmentLine $AA62, and for each of the D fragments takes a free actor
> record (FindFreeActor $8BE3; it stops quietly when none is free), random parameters (RandomFragmentParams $AA70)
> and starts it (InitFragment $AA7E). IY is kept.
> Stage 1's SpawnFragments at $A846 is the same code.
