@module actors
$AC0A c SetActorFrame ; Set the actor IY to frame A of a frame table (the 4 bytes after the CALL)
> The CALL is followed by two words: the frame table DE and the graphics base BC; the routine pops them and
> returns to its caller's caller. A frame record is 6 bytes (FrameRecordAddress $B1BE: DE + 6A): +0 the column
> offset (negated when the actor faces left, +9 bit 7), +1 the line offset, +2 the width in bytes, +3 the height in
> lines, +4/+5 the offset of the image from the graphics base. The actor's column +0 = the offset + its base column
> +$0D, its line +1 = the line offset + its base line +$0E, +2 and +3 the size, +4/+5 the image address. An image is
> width x height bytes, row by row, one bit a pixel, no mask (DrawSprite $B4EA copies it).
> Stage 1's SetActorFrame at $AA02 is the same code.
> Witness: L1 14148 (rzx-r3, s3-right).

@module hero
$AC46 c HeroActor ; Per-pass handler of the hero's record ($74E0): move, fall, leave the room, change grid
> The handler word of the hero's template ($9C76), called first in each pass of UpdateActors $A7BB with IY =
> $74E0. HeroUpdate $ADE3 (controls and states), CheckHeroFooting $AC6F (ledges and falls), CheckRoomExits $ACE2
> with IX = RoomExitsPtr $FE2E, CheckGridPassages $AD24, then RoomExitsPtr = the grid record's word +4 +
> RoomNumber $FE30 (the room may have changed).
> Stage 1's HeroActor at $AA3E is the same code.
> Witness: L1 6280 (rzx-r3, s3-right).
$AC6F c CheckHeroFooting ; Catch a ledge in a jump, or start a fall where the ground ends
> IY = the hero. In a jump (state 2) at frame `$0C`: solid ground under the feet one column ahead (CellUnderFeet `$B1C8`, E = 1, D = 2) lands him on the ledge: frame `$0F`, the base column 2 back (MoveBaseX `$B1A6`), the base line 16 up (MoveActorY `$963E`), on into JumpFrame `$B13D`; at frame `$0F` with no ground there he drops (StartDrop `$AFB6`). Standing (state 0) or walking (state 1) at frame 5 or `$0B` with no ground under him (E = 1, D = 2, C = 7) starts a fall (StartFall `$AFA4`).
> Stage 1's CheckHeroFooting tested the ground of the stand and the walk with E = 2, D = 0. Called by HeroActor `$AC46` every pass.
> Witness: L1 6280 (rzx-r3, s3-right).
$AC96 CheckHeroFootingState
