@module graphics ; The stage's tiles and map, sprites, pictures and their frame tables
@about Every animated actor shows frames of a sprite set: the bitmaps, then a frame table of 6-byte records (dx, dy, the width in bytes, the height in lines, the bitmap's offset from the set's start). SetActorFrame $AC0A takes the frame number in A and the table and the set's start from the two words after its CALL. The frames are 1 bit a pixel, rows top first, no mask, ORed into the play buffer (mirrored through BitReverse for an actor facing left). Each set's bitmaps are exactly the bytes its frames cover, the table right after them (one exception: DragonHeadSprites, one stray byte before its table).
@about Stage 3's sets: the hero's walk, jump, leap and strikes (a hammer); the urns and chests; the pieces of the artefact; the Viking warrior; the troll; the bog man; the dragon's head and its breath; the drawbridge; the pyre's flames, bier and body; and the pictures drawn without a table: the lightning bolts, the dragon (a row-packed picture with its colours), the seated figure of the castle hall (the same), the water's ripple, the shots, the fireballs, the thrown objects, the item icons, GAME OVER, the burst's glyphs and shapes.
$B556 b StageGraphics 16 ; The stage's tiles, blocks and map, RLE-packed (3231 bytes; 4437 unpacked: 229 tiles, 118 blocks, the three grids' map)
> RoomChange unpacks it with Unrle $A39A into the play buffer at $5B00 at every room change (the buffer is cleared again before the actors are drawn). Unrle: the first byte is the escape ($F9 here); a byte other than the escape is itself, ESC n v is n copies of v, ESC ESC ends. Unpacked: five words, the offsets from $5B0A of the tile kinds (0), the tiles' pixels ($E5: 229 x 8 bytes), their attributes ($080D), the blocks ($08F2: 118 x 4 tile numbers) and the map ($0ACA: grid 0 47 x 9, grid 1 124 x 9, grid 2 14 x 9 block numbers, at the grid records' map offsets 0, $01A7, $0603).
> The packer that made it is greedy: every run of 4 to 255 equal bytes is ESC n v, except one stretch of 8 zero bytes left as they are (unpacked offset 1663: a blank tile's pixels). With that one exception tools/res_stage.py packs the block again bit for bit (graphics.txt, tiles.png). All 3231 bytes read in rzx-r3 and s3-right (each room change).
@res stage3/graphics.bin
$C1F5 b LightningBolt1 2 ; The shortest lightning bolt: 2 bytes x 24 lines
> The four bolts are drawn by the lightning (kind $0C) through LightningShapes $9500 (the bitmap, the width, the height of each, and a blank 1 x 1 for no bolt). All four read in rzx-r3 and s3-right (the deck of the longship).
@res stage3/bitmaps-lightning-1-2x24.bin
$C225 b LightningBolt2 2 ; A lightning bolt: 2 bytes x 48 lines
@res stage3/bitmaps-lightning-2-2x48.bin
